itcoin  musk has tweeted about other  cryptocurrencies as well  take the once joke crypto dogecoin and  it keeps climbing  the meme inspired cryptocurrency nearing  nearly doubling over  the past week alone this ahead of elon  musk's appearance on  snl early on may 8th before musk was  slated to host an episode of saturday  night live  dogecoin was trading around 73 cents  investors had been pumping money into  the cryptocurrency  based on speculation that it could  finally reach a dollar  but that didn't happen during a skid he  performed in the guise of a financial  expert  the self-proclaimed doge father jokingly  explained what dogecoin is  it's a cryptocurrency you can trade for  conventional money  oh so it's a hustle yeah it's awesome  by the time the episode ended the price  of the crypto had plummeted around 30  percent  that comment alone rattled the  confidence that people had that dogecoin  could keep pushing higher  and people took profits and all of a  sudden it sold off but then  two weeks later musk tweeted a picture  of a shiba inu on a dollar  with the question how much is that doge  in the window  following his tweet the price spiked  dogecoin unlike bitcoin  doesn't really have an investment case  and that means that  dogecoin is really just a cryptocurrency  built on memes  the only reason it has any value at all  at the moment  is because elon musk first started  caring about it and then snoop dogg  started caring about it  and then all of these other like rappers  and celebrities started tweeting about  dogecoin  well these are two of the most recent  examples of musk influencing crypto  there are many more and there are other  forces at play  that have allowed musk to amass the  influence he has on crypto  over the last year there has been a  flood of new retail investors  largely driven by the rise in no fee  trading apps like robin hood  malcolm demirs an executive at the asset  management firm coin shares  says that no fee trading apps have  increased the popularity of crypto  because people can access more types of  assets on the same platform  it's also made really illiquid  cryptocurrencies of the past  much more liquid because there's now  much more retail participation  some experts say younger people  gravitate towards musk because they like  his idea of the future and see him as  rebellious  and demure says that musk's huge twitter  following is a big part of his influence  he has over 56 million followers  financial markets to some people  are a form of entertainment and so i  think what we are  seeing is the gamification of clout on  social media  where people are recognizing that they  can manipulate markets using social  media as a tool  but she says musk's influence on the  crypto market has downsides  there is a wide range of ways through  which market participants are are acting  on their desire to to buy and sell  cryptocurrencies  and as a result what we see is more  liquidity but also  more volatility when people like elon  musk are tweeting directly  to retail all assets are subject to ups  and downs  but as you can see from the big swings  on this chart crypto is especially  volatile  all of a sudden elon has reminded people  no this isn't just going up in a  straight line  it does come down and when it does it  can be fast  these market swings can have a very real  impact on retail investors  but for some the risk is worth it  because there's no fundamentals  it makes it really hard to try and  figure out where the floor is like where  the  fair value um and where the sell-off  should stop when it happens  and so you inherently wind up having a  much more volatile market  which is what appeals to some investors  for this like they don't want the steady  returns of  the s p where they have to wait you know  30 years to  get where they want to be they want to  get these fast  sharp returns some experts think that  musk's influence on bitcoin may be  waning  but for now his tweets continue to send  shock waves through the crypto market
 

